{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Among the godless</b> — Some say: that the godless say a thing to mock them, the masters of cakes, and this interpretation is far-fetched and has no reason. And what is near to me: that these godless, who are godless of mockery, mockery is in their eyes like a cake to eat, in the manner of: \"Those who eat my people eat bread\" (Micah 3:3), therefore above, \"they tore my flesh.\" And the proof that this is so is what comes after it: \"they gnash their teeth at me.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:40.960537223Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}